{"budapest":{"id":"a7e457a4-152a-429b-8be4-668a2105e878","word":"Budapest","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"the capital city of Hungary","word":"Budapeste"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"A week later, Orbán was discussing the theory with American allies at a special meeting of the Conservative Political Action Committee (Cpac), a rightwing American group, in Budapest. Cpac’s chairman, Matt Schlapp, even suggested outlawing abortion as a solution: “If you’re worried about this ‘replacement’, why don’t we start there? Start with allowing our own people to live.”","ref":"2022 June 8, Steve Rose, “A deadly ideology: how the ‘great replacement theory’ went mainstream”, in The Guardian, archived from the original on 31 Mar 2023:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[174,182]],"id":"27b8c64a-d3a2-4926-b00f-50819e84a8b1"}],"wikidata":["Q1781"],"senseid":["en:Q1781"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Budapest","en:Cities in Hungary","en:National capitals","en:Places in Hungary"],"links":[["capital","capital"],["populous","populous"],["Hungary","Hungary#English"]],"glosses":["The capital and the most populous city of Hungary."],"id":"c70dcb12-0927-4930-8b0a-34af3e456e16"},{"examples":[{"text":"After information about the secret proceedings between Berlin and Budapest leaked, Rome approached Budapest to get details on the concessions granted with the envisaged German–Hungarian commercial contract.","ref":"2016, Per Tiedtke, chapter 8, in Germany, Italy and the International Economy 1929–1936: Co-operation or Rivalries at Times of Crisis?, Europe: Tectum Verlag, →ISBN, page 265:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[66,74],[99,107]],"id":"fdbe7e3c-3f79-4d1a-95fc-e17208fe9df1"}],"categories":["English metonyms","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["Hungarian","Hungarian"],["government","government"]],"raw_glosses":["(metonymic) The Hungarian government."],"glosses":["The Hungarian govern