with usage examples","English transitive verbs"],"links":[["plan","plan"],["use","use"]],"raw_glosses":["(transitive) To plan for the use of in a budget."],"glosses":["To plan for the use of in a budget."],"tags":["transitive"],"id":"1c0bf465-f2e2-495b-977c-6ecf5effff05"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"buddy":{"id":"5ed6dddc-7ec6-42d5-9982-3f11d29b65f1","word":"buddy","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"friend or casual acquaintance","tags":["masculine"],"word":"companheiro"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"partner for a particular activity","tags":["feminine","masculine"],"word":"colega"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"informal address to a stranger","tags":["masculine"],"word":"parceiro"}],"pos":"pron","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"I found some earphones in the pocket, buddy must have been pissed.","bold_text_offsets":[[38,43]],"type":"example","id":"0c9fb000-45a3-49c6-9a8c-b751720c096c"},{"text":"Buddy's loaded. 'Got like three houses.","bold_text_offsets":[[0,5]],"type":"example","id":"6fd5a79f-6998-4bc0-a000-b8ae75330dff"}],"raw_glosses":["(Maritime English) A person far removed from the conversation."],"qualifier":"Maritime English","glosses":["A person far removed from the conversation."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"9924f92c-c6b1-4645-83f6-98964f1de712"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"budge":{"id":"4f2b2866-b2c4-4527-a7fb-83f604633359","word":"budge","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"intransitive: to move","word":"mover-se"}],"pos":"verb","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"I’ve been pushing this rock as hard as I can, but it won’t budge an inch.","bold_text_offsets":[[59,64]],"type":"example","id":"da94e9f1-0f07-42a5-b28d-77a043de58dc"},{"text":"Ile not budge an inch boy: Let him come, and kindly.","ref":"c. 1590–1592 (date written), William Shakespeare, “The Taming of the Shrew”, in Mr. William Shakespeares Comedies, Histories, & Tragedies […] (First Folio), London: […] Isaac Iaggard, and Ed[ward] Blount, published 1623, →OCLC, [Act I, scene i], page 208, column 1:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[8,13]],"id":"795ff5a3-c912-4860-b5fb-9e0da3cd2ed2"},{"text":"[…]although his ſouldiers were much moved and offended to ſee their fellowes put to the worſt, he could not be induced to bouge from his place[…]","ref":"1603, Michel de Montaigne, “Of the batell of Dreux”, in John Florio, transl., The Essayes […], book I, London: […] Val[entine] Simmes for Edward Blount […], →OCLC, page 148:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[122,127]],"id":"368d6fbe-ecbe-4a7c-9890-d890c9cf5465"},{"text":"Yet goals in either half from Jordi Gómez and James Perch inspired them and then, in the face of a relentless City onslaught, they simply would not budge, throwing heart, body and soul in the way of a ball which seemed destined for their net on several occasions.","ref":"2014 March 9, Jacob Steinberg, “Wigan shock Manchester City in FA Cup again to reach semi-finals”, in The Guardian:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[148,153]],"id":"a28dddc1-ab4d-4c19-9d80-3f3aac176839"},{"text":"The gender equality picture stateside can also seem bleak, especially in the wake of the Supreme Court gutting reproductive rights last summer. Women still make only 83 percent of what men do in the U.S.—a stat that has barely budged in the past 20 years.","ref":"2023 March 13, Naureen Khan, “Doug Emhoff Wants Men to Clear the Path for More Kamalas”, in Cosmopolitan:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[227,233]],"id":"5833d936-6dbc-40fe-9d97-dbd4c2474913"}],"categories":["English intransitive verbs","English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"links":[["move","move"]],"raw_glosses":["(intransitive) To move; to be shifted from a fixed position."],"glosses":["To move; to be shifted from a fixed position."],"tags":["intransitive"],"id":"0c58f2c1-2dd1-41a7-af0a-dc03c41ef883"},{"examples":[{"text":"I’ve been pushing this rock as hard as I can, but I can’t budge it.","bold_text_offsets":[[58,63]],"type":"example","id":"74484cf0-c389-4e71-80ea-0266644df16d"}],"categories":["English terms with usage examples","English transitive verbs"],"raw_glosses":["(transitive) To move; to shift from a fixed position."],"glosses":["To move; to shift from a fixed position."],"tags":["transitive"],"id":"96562fcc-8bef-41e3-8280-66f6c9631fd3"},{"examples":[{"text":"The Minister for Finance refused to budge on the new economic rules.","bold_text_offsets":[[36,41]],"type":"example","id":"d2c8e304-d206-4718-bf63-ae17ede09467"},{"text":"If only I could get Ambrose to take me away somewhere! But he won't budge.","ref":"1933, Richard Curle, Corruption, page 75:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[68,73]],"id":"38bd9e2d-1a4e-44f4-bbad-cb3e919240c7"}],"links":[["opinion","opinion"],["belief","belief"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"glosses":["To yield in one’s opinions or beliefs."],"id":"159f6891-1cae-47d0-9f0f-bd07429cc3c0"},{"examples":[{"text":"Hey, no budging! Don't budge in line!","bold_text_offsets":[[8,15],[23,28]],"type":"example","id":"894e017b-de77-4a7f-9ded-0f9e88459574"}],"categories":["Canadian English","English terms with usage examples","Indiana English","Upper Midwestern US English"],"links":[["cut","cut"],["butt","butt"]],"raw_glosses":["(Upper Midwestern US, Indiana, western Canada) To cut or butt (in line); to join the front or middle rather than the back of a queue."],"qualifier":"Upper Midwestern US; Indiana; Upper Midwestern US; Indiana","glosses":["To cut or butt (in line); to join the front or middle rather than the back of a queue."],"tags":["Canada","Western"],"id":"4ad82283-15f1-4fed-9947-5df1d9e20132"},{"links":[["improve","improve"],["spot","spot"]],"glosses":["To try to improve the spot of a decision on a sports field."],"id":"354a1e6a-7b6f-42f6-b853-989fe75b9aa1"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"word":"shift"}]},"buddha's hand":{"id":"0c819032-e432-45a4-966b-0f6a3b9a5f49","word":"Buddha's hand","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"citrus fruit","tags":["feminine"],"word":"cidra-mão-de-buda"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"categories":["Cantonese terms with redundant transliterations","English countable nouns","English entries with incorrect language header","English eponyms","English lemmas","English multiword terms","English nouns","Entries using missing taxonomic name (variety)","Entries with translation boxes","Mandarin terms with redundant transliterations","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Cantonese translations","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with Esperanto translations","Terms with Estonian translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Japanese translations","Terms with Korean translations","Terms with Macanese translations","Terms with Mandarin translations","Terms with Mongolian translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Spanish translations","Terms with Thai translations","Terms with Vietnamese translations","en:Citrus subfamily plants","en:Fruits"],"links":[["citron","citron"]],"glosses":["Citrus medica var. sarcodactylus, a fragrant variant of citron whose fruit is segmented into finger-like sections."],"id":"c1139747-e3d5-41d6-8868-32e5f34ec913"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"sense":"Buddha's Hand citron, fingered citron","word":"Citrus medica var. sarcodactylus"}]},"budgetary":{"id":"01adf715-ffc3-4656-99e8-bc3aa9fbd8fb","word":"budgetary","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"of or pertaining to a budget","tags":["masculine"],"word":"orçamentário"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Jap